60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Candidate A is too risky given the visit completion rates and funding. D is too slow legally.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"A and D fail the logistics test. B and C are on-site, but C requires more space.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"B is joint-run, which is a red flag, but D's data agreements are a total non-starter.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"B uses midwifery, and I saw they have slack! C uses therapy, but they are losing staff.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"B is on-site and billable. C is also on-site, but the staffing review is concerning.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"I vote for B. It is the most viable, provided the midwifery slack is utilized.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,I agree. B fits the physical constraints better than a new rehab unit.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I have reservations about joint clinics, but B is better than the others.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I love B! It helps parents and uses the staff who can actually handle it.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,It seems B is the most harmonious choice for our current budget and personnel.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
